  ('justinminchow402_c01', 'justinminchow402', '@kelly_moo82', 'We can have empathy without letting it rule us. It’s OK to feel badly that people are being sent back to their home country which isn’t as awesome as ours but we can’t let that deter us from having rules.', 0, 1),
  ('justinminchow402_c02', 'justinminchow402', '@daniel_lan58', 'hey they just caught 244 people in texas exploiting children! most of them look like you and me', 0, 2),
  ('justinminchow402_c03', 'justinminchow402', '@johnsonjeffery', 'well said', 0, 3),
  ('justinminchow402_c04', 'justinminchow402', '@samuel87', 'Why aren''t you fed up with corrupt politicians who advocate for hostile govt actions, felons in the White House, unchecked police brutality, the rapidly growing homless population, the growing ceo/worker wage gap, corporate wage theft, and a plethora of other homegrown problems affecting Americans much more harshly than everything you rattled off. Maybe it''s because you fell for the propaganda & ignored the fact that immigrants are far less likely to commit crimes than Americans are.', 0, 4),
  ('justinminchow402_c05', 'justinminchow402', '@chad34', 'I’m fed up with paying taxes so that everybody else can get handouts. Whether they’re immigrants or citizens.', 0, 5),
  ('justinminchow402_c06', 'justinminchow402', '@david.p4', 'When you voted for a felon who''s disobeying court orders and our constitution don''t get on here and say you''re for law and order😂😂😂 its racism plain and simple. what about the 600k candadians living here undocumented, not a peep huh?', 0, 6),
  ('justinminchow402_c07', 'justinminchow402', '@aboutseven218', 'Exactly!! I do feel bad for the people getting deported who haven’t done anything wrong other than entering our country illegally, especially if they were fleeing from their own country due to it being dangerous, but I have to put my country and its citizens first. We need documented immigrants who’ve been proven safe for our country. With how many undocumented are in our borders it’s understandable why they went the deportation route. Too many people to run a background check on, and that lets the dangerous people have more time to do harm. It’s quicker and safer to do the mass deportations. I hate it, but like I said, I’m putting my country first.', 0, 7),
  ('justinminchow402_c08', 'justinminchow402', '@michaeljones', 'remember class: not having papers ❌ two impeachments, 34 felonies, countless fraud convictions, and being best buds with multiple high profile pedos ✅✅✅', 0, 8),
  ('justinminchow402_c09', 'justinminchow402', '@michaeljones', 'When you’re a gang member in my country, bringing destruction and violence and you are also illegal… I don’t care where you’re sent as long as it’s not here. And prison sounds like an excellent place for violent criminals.', 0, 9),
  ('justinminchow402_c10', 'justinminchow402', '@julie.r5', 'Thank you so much I’ve been trying to explain this to people', 0, 10);
